@jebrosen I believe this is in sufficient condition to merge.

I just tested it locally with a `/shutdown` route, which included a 15 second delay to allow requesting other routes in the meantime. The server successfully stayed alive while waiting for the 15 seconds to expire (before responding), and acted like it was shut down for any new requests.

Here's the full code if you'd like to test it yourself.

```rust
#![feature(proc_macro_hygiene, async_await)]

use futures::compat::Future01CompatExt; // futures-preview
use rocket::{get, routes, shutdown::ShutdownHandle};
use std::time::{Duration, Instant};
use tokio::timer::Delay;

async fn sleep(secs: u64) {
    Delay::new(Instant::now() + Duration::from_secs(secs))
        .compat()
        .await
        .unwrap()
}

#[get("/immediate")]
fn immediate() {}

#[get("/shutdown")]
async fn shutdown(handle: &ShutdownHandle<'_>) {
    handle.shutdown();
    sleep(15).await;
}

fn main() {
    let _ = rocket::ignite()
        .mount("/", routes![shutdown, immediate])
        .launch();
}
```

