This is intended behavior - all windows and panels are auto-shrinking. In most cases this is the desired behavior, but if the egui user doesn't like it, they can do `ui.allocate_space(ui.available_size());` themselves.

As for expandable panels, this should work:

``` rust
        egui::TopBottomPanel::top("top_panel")
            .resizable(true)
            .min_height(32.0)
            .show_inside(ui, |ui| {
                egui::ScrollArea::auto_sized().show(ui, |ui| {
                    ui.vertical_centered(|ui| {
                        ui.heading("Expandable Upper Panel");
