Oh, great! I missed it. In `Utf8Chunked`, do you recommend to use apply directly?

`trim_matches` supports trimming all prefixes and suffixes that match a pattern repeatedly.

Citing [rust document examples](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/string/struct.String.html#method.trim_right_matches),

```rust
assert_eq!("11foo1bar11".trim_matches('1'), "foo1bar");
assert_eq!("123foo1bar123".trim_matches(char::is_numeric), "foo1bar");

let x: &[_] = &['1', '2'];
assert_eq!("12foo1bar12".trim_matches(x), "foo1bar");
assert_eq!("1foo1barXX".trim_matches(|c| c == '1' || c == 'X'), "foo1bar");
```

