Yes, it's here:
```rust
            if used && (ep.ep_type == EndpointType::Isochronous || ep.ep_type == EndpointType::Bulk) {
                 // Isochronous and bulk endpoints are double-buffered.
                 // Their corresponding endpoint/channel registers are forced to be unidirectional.
                 // Do not reuse this index.
                 return false;
             }
```

It is necessary to fix allocation for double-buffered endpoints, e.g. ISO. For single-buffered bulk endpoints, I later took back this change. I guess it was not released yet.

See https://github.com/embassy-rs/embassy/blob/main/embassy-stm32/src/usb/usb.rs#L381

So it should work again on `main` and when the next release comes.

