ReferenceError: ArrayFinalization is not defined

I've got a custom structure called `Array`:

```rust
#[wasm_bindgen]
pub struct Array {

}

#[wasm_bindgen]
impl Array {
  #[wasm_bindgen(constructor)]
  pub fn new() -> Self {
    Self {}
  }
}
```

When initialising a corresponding class in the JavaScript code via `new mylib.Array()`, it fails with the following error:

```
  ReferenceError: ArrayFinalization is not defined
      at new Array2 (/path/to/mylib.js:444:9)
```

After looking into generated js code, I can notice following thing: since the `Array` is already an existing name of the type, my custom type is aliased into `Array2` and wasm-bindgen generates a registry called `Array2Finalization`:

```js
const Array2Finalization = (typeof FinalizationRegistry === 'undefined')
    ? { register: () => {}, unregister: () => {} }
    : new FinalizationRegistry(ptr => wasm.__wbg_array_free(ptr >>> 0, 1));
```

However the code for the custom Array constructor uses an un-aliased registry name (which doesn't exist):

```js
class Array2 {
    constructor(items) {
        var ptr0 = isLikeNone(items) ? 0 : passArrayJsValueToWasm0(items, wasm.__wbindgen_malloc);
        var len0 = WASM_VECTOR_LEN;
        const ret = wasm.array_new(ptr0, len0);
        this.__wbg_ptr = ret >>> 0;
        ArrayFinalization.register(this, this.__wbg_ptr, this);   // ArrayFinalization doesn't exist, Array2Finalization should be used instead
        return this;
    }
}
```

It seems that alias is not used in the constructor. Unfortunately for compatibility reasons, I cannot use other naming.

