Even if this is the desired behavior, documentation should be clear about it.
Currently, it is not obvious that it would happen from the example in [the docs](https://github.com/rust-lang-nursery/rustfmt/blob/master/Configurations.md#merge_imports).

### Current docs:

`false` (default):
```
use foo::{a, c, d};
use foo::{b, g};
use foo::{e, f};
```
`true`:
```
use foo::{a, b, c, d, e, f, g};
```

### Possible example that shows all the differences:
`false` (default):
```
use foo::{a, c, d};
use foo::{b, g};
use bar::{e, f};
```
`true`:
```
use {
    foo::{a, b, c, d, g},
    bar::{e, f},
};
```

